# The #529 ptrint census baseline — scripts/ptrint_census.sh gate mode.
#
# MEASURED, not chosen: `places` is the distinct seam places the census reported over src/, lib/ and
# every tracked fixture on main at 7aae8b3 (1 BIND i2p + 2 RESULT-TAIL p2i, all in test/, all OUTSIDE
# an `unchecked` grant); `blind-lib` is the tracked lib/ modules the census could NOT check standalone,
# so their places are unknown rather than zero.
#
# Neither number may grow.
#
# `op-cmp` IS now claimed clean, and held: the planted fixture plants a pointer meeting an integer
# literal — granted, because MEM-9 (Memory §4.5, spec v1.6.0) makes the ungranted form ill-formed and a
# refused planted program cannot prove anything (`planted` fails on it by design) — `planted` reports the
# hook PROVEN (`proven=13/13` — every class, OP-CMP included), and the census reports `op-cmp=0` over
# src/, lib/ and every tracked fixture. The ratchet holds that 0 and REFUSES to hold it while the hook is
# unproven — an unproven zero is silence, not cleanliness, so the ceiling returns rc=2 rather than
# passing. An earlier revision of this file said OP-CMP could not be claimed because its hook sat
# undispatched under the bootstrap seed ("scar #2"); that was false — both the tree compiler and
# `seed/alatyr 0.2.16` fire it on `p == 0`.
#
# WHAT THIS 0 MEANS AFTER MEM-9, stated so the next agent does not over-read it: it counts crossings the
# census SEES among programs it accepts. Once MEM-9 lands, no accepted program may contain an ungranted
# pointer-meeting-integer comparison at all, so this zero stops being a survey result and becomes a
# consequence of the rule — it is no longer evidence that such sites were looked for and not found. The
# evidence that the refusal fires is #1034's `reject_ptr_eq_int_outside_grant.al`, a different assertion
# in a different instrument; the evidence that the census still SEES a crossing when one is legal is the
# granted planted row above, which must keep reporting OP-CMP proven.
# places=5, measured on native x86_64 (omen) at main + #1034 + #1082 by
# `bash scripts/ptrint_census.sh census target/debug/alatyr`: 3 -> 5, and the two new places are named
# in that run's grant table — `test/accept_ptr_eq_int_unchecked_grant.al` and
# `test/reject_ptr_eq_int_outside_grant.al`, one OP-CMP each. They are #1034's own fixtures, the pair
# that proves MEM-9 fires where it must and does not fire where it must not, so the census counting them
# is the instrument working, not a regression. They are NOT excluded: a census blind to the fixtures that
# test its own rule would be blind where it matters most (I4). `op-cmp=0` is unchanged and still means
# what the paragraph above says it means after MEM-9 — zero ungranted crossings among accepted programs.
places=5
blind-lib=12
op-cmp=0
